1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,846
CareOneX 分成两半
CareOneX has two halves.

2
00:00:02,166 --> 00:00:05,398
一半在电话里和家属对话
One half talks to a family on the phone.

3
00:00:05,718 --> 00:00:09,309
另一半在任何来电之前就已经运行
The other half runs long before any call:

4
00:00:09,309 --> 00:00:13,775
它搭建一座资料库，每个回答都从这里来
it builds the library that every answer comes from.

5
00:00:14,017 --> 00:00:16,479
这一集讲资料库：五个容器（container）
This episode is about the library:

6
00:00:16,479 --> 00:00:21,909
把 20 份公开文档变成 232 段可以检索的文字
five containers that turn 20 public documents into 232 searchable passages.

7
00:00:22,150 --> 00:00:24,148
为什么要先建资料库？
Why build a library at all?

8
00:00:24,468 --> 00:00:31,232
来电者问到收入上限时，agent，也就是电话里的 AI 助手
When a caller asks about an income limit, the agent, the AI assistant on the phone,

9
00:00:31,232 --> 00:00:34,329
必须根据官方文件回答
must answer from an official document.

10
00:00:34,649 --> 00:00:41,354
它不能凭记忆回答，因为这些数字每年都会变
It is not allowed to answer from memory, because these numbers change every year.

11
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:45,378
所以每个回答都从这样一段文字开始
So every answer starts as one of these passages.

12
00:00:45,698 --> 00:00:51,302
我们跟着一份文档，依次走过这五个容器
Let's follow a document through the five containers, one at a time.

13
00:00:52,350 --> 00:00:56,157
一切从一张表格开始：来源清单（source list）
Everything starts with one spreadsheet, the source list.

14
00:00:56,477 --> 00:01:00,242
它列出了团队批准的 20 份公开文档
It names 20 public documents that the team approved.

15
00:01:00,483 --> 00:01:05,379
一半以上来自新泽西州老龄服务司（DoAS）
More than half come from New Jersey's Division of Aging Services.

16
00:01:05,699 --> 00:01:09,326
其余来自 Medicaid、Medicare、退伍军人
The rest come from Medicaid, Medicare, Veterans Affairs and Disability Services.

17
00:01:09,326 --> 00:01:11,781
事务部（VA）和残障服务司
The rest come from Medicaid, Medicare, Veterans Affairs and Disability Services.

18
00:01:12,101 --> 00:01:14,417
其中 11 份是网页，8 份是 PDF
11 are web pages, 8 are PDFs,

19
00:01:14,417 --> 00:01:19,688
还有 1 份是团队根据州政府 2026 年的文件整理的摘要
and 1 is a summary the team wrote from the state's 2026 documents.

20
00:01:19,933 --> 00:01:23,708
每一行都记着回答以后要用到的信息
Each row carries what an answer needs later:

21
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:28,942
项目名称、网址、规则生效的日期
the program, the web address, the date the rules took effect,

22
00:01:28,942 --> 00:01:32,803
以及文件的“指纹”，也就是 hash（哈希值）
and a fingerprint of the file, called a hash.

23
00:01:33,050 --> 00:01:36,677
来源清单是整条 pipeline 唯一的输入
The source list is the pipeline's only input.

24
00:01:36,997 --> 00:01:40,895
要加一份文档，就加一行再重新 build
To add a document, you add a row and rebuild,

25
00:01:40,895 --> 00:01:45,920
因为这张清单是打包进 data 容器镜像里的
because the list is built into the data container's image.

26
00:01:46,967 --> 00:01:48,989
S3 是亚马逊的文件存储服务
S3 is Amazon's file storage.

27
00:01:49,309 --> 00:01:52,381
bucket（存储桶）是里面最顶层的一个文件夹
A bucket is one top-level folder in it,

28
00:01:52,381 --> 00:01:55,612
里面的每个文件叫 object（对象）
and each file inside is called an object.

29
00:01:55,932 --> 00:02:00,781
第一个容器 data 负责确保团队的 bucket 存在
The first container, data, makes sure the team's bucket exists.

30
00:02:01,101 --> 00:02:08,051
它会保留每个文件的旧版本，做了加密，而且只存放公开文档
It keeps old versions of every file, it is encrypted, and it holds public documents only.

31
00:02:08,371 --> 00:02:11,601
来电者的任何信息都不会放进去
No caller information ever goes into it.

32
00:02:11,850 --> 00:02:14,438
它的名字以 ac215 开头，是有意为之
Its name starts with ac215 on purpose.

33
00:02:14,758 --> 00:02:20,342
团队的 S3 权限只覆盖名字以 ac215 开头的 bucket
The team's S3 permissions only reach buckets whose names start with ac215,

34
00:02:20,342 --> 00:02:22,228
所以这门课里的任何东西都碰不到
so nothing in this course

35
00:02:22,228 --> 00:02:27,435
公司以 careonex 命名的生产环境 bucket
can touch the company's production buckets, which are named careonex.

36
00:02:27,684 --> 00:02:33,366
第二个容器 ingest 下载每一份文档，并计算它的 hash
The second container, ingest, downloads every document and computes its hash.

37
00:02:33,686 --> 00:02:38,291
如果 bucket 里已经有同样 hash 的文件，就跳过
If the bucket already holds a file with that hash, it skips it.

38
00:02:38,611 --> 00:02:41,458
否则就上传新版本
Otherwise it uploads the new version.

39
00:02:41,700 --> 00:02:46,225
它还会在每个文件旁边写一个小的元数据文件
Next to every file it writes a small sidecar of metadata:

40
00:02:46,225 --> 00:02:50,434
叫 sidecar：项目、年份、州、生效日期
the program, the year, the state, the effective date.

41
00:02:50,754 --> 00:02:55,927
之后检索时就能按这些字段过滤，比如只看 JACC
Later, search can filter on these fields, for example only JACC.

42
00:02:56,167 --> 00:02:58,758
每次运行还会写一份 manifest（清单）
Every run also writes a manifest:

43
00:02:58,758 --> 00:03:01,507
准确记录它看到了哪些文件版本
exactly which file versions it saw.

44
00:03:01,827 --> 00:03:05,869
这份 manifest 就是整个数据集的版本号
That manifest is the version of the whole dataset.

45
00:03:06,917 --> 00:03:11,016
做这期视频时，我们做了一个测试
Here is something we tested while making this video.

46
00:03:11,336 --> 00:03:14,188
我们把每份文档都下载了两次
We downloaded every document twice,

47
00:03:14,188 --> 00:03:17,937
间隔几秒钟，方式和 ingest 完全一样
a few seconds apart, the same way ingest does.

48
00:03:18,257 --> 00:03:20,782
8 份 PDF 两次都一模一样
All 8 PDFs came back identical,

49
00:03:20,782 --> 00:03:24,692
而且仍然和来源清单里的 hash 对得上
and still matched their hash in the source list.

50
00:03:25,012 --> 00:03:31,099
但 11 个网页里有 5 个，第二次下载回来的字节不一样
But 5 of the 11 web pages came back with different bytes the second time.

51
00:03:31,334 --> 00:03:34,473
这些网页上的文字其实没有变
The text on those pages had not changed.

52
00:03:34,793 --> 00:03:41,813
在 nj.gov 上，页面末尾有时会多出一段带随机数的防爬虫脚本
On nj.gov, a bot-protection script with a random number is sometimes added at the end.

53
00:03:42,133 --> 00:03:43,413
在 va.gov 上
On va.gov,

54
00:03:43,413 --> 00:03:49,321
每次都会给几十个标签打上一个新的随机码，叫 nonce
a fresh random code, called a nonce, is stamped on dozens of tags every time.

55
00:03:49,641 --> 00:03:55,968
所以，下载文件的 hash 没法告诉你规则有没有变
So the hash of a downloaded file cannot tell you whether the rules changed.

56
00:03:56,217 --> 00:03:57,851
这正是 extract 的任务
That is extract's job.

57
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:02,948
它把每个文件转成干净的文本，格式是 Markdown
It turns every file into clean text, written as Markdown:

58
00:04:02,948 --> 00:04:08,898
纯文本加上几个表示结构的符号，比如标题前面加一个 #
plain text with a few symbols for structure, like a # before a heading.

59
00:04:09,218 --> 00:04:15,421
这段文本的 hash，才是文档内容真正变化的信号
The hash of that text is the real signal that a document's content moved.

60
00:04:15,667 --> 00:04:18,716
网页的处理改了三个版本才做对
Getting web pages right took three versions.

61
00:04:19,036 --> 00:04:23,063
第 1 版用了一个自动“猜”正文的库
Version 1 used a library that guesses the main content,

62
00:04:23,063 --> 00:04:26,504
结果悄悄丢掉了讲申请资格的段落
and it silently dropped eligibility paragraphs.

63
00:04:26,824 --> 00:04:33,726
第 2 版先删导航栏，可 nj.gov 把整个页面包在导航栏里面
Version 2 deleted navigation first, but nj.gov wraps the whole page inside its navigation bar,

64
00:04:33,726 --> 00:04:35,489
结果页面变成空的
so pages came out empty.

65
00:04:35,809 --> 00:04:40,301
第 3 版先找到正文区域，然后才做删除
Version 3 finds the main region first, and only then strips.

66
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:44,074
PDF 交给一个叫 pymupdf4llm 的库处理
PDFs go through a library called pymupdf4llm.

67
00:04:44,394 --> 00:04:49,455
它保留标题，并把表格转成 Markdown 表格
It keeps headings, and it turns tables into Markdown tables,

68
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:53,420
这样一个数字就和它的标签留在同一行
so a number stays in the same row as its label.

69
00:04:54,467 --> 00:04:58,100
检索不该把一份 22 页的指南整个丢给 agent
Search should not hand the agent a 22-page guide.

70
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:02,756
它应该返回一段文字：短到一眼能读完
It should return a passage short enough to read at once,

71
00:05:02,756 --> 00:05:06,086
又具体到能回答一个问题
and specific enough to answer one question.

72
00:05:06,406 --> 00:05:11,862
所以 chunk 容器把每份文档切成小块，叫 chunk（文本块）
So the chunk container cuts every document into pieces called chunks.

73
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:15,229
第一条规则：每个标题开始一个新的 chunk
Rule one: a heading starts a new chunk,

74
00:05:15,229 --> 00:05:19,241
而且每个 chunk 都带着它完整的标题路径
and every chunk carries its full path of headings.

75
00:05:19,561 --> 00:05:22,292
这样，“收入上限 4,855 美元”
So the line "income limit 4,855 dollars" never travels without the word JACC.

76
00:05:22,292 --> 00:05:25,875
这一行就永远不会和 JACC 这个词分开
So the line "income limit 4,855 dollars" never travels without the word JACC.

77
00:05:26,117 --> 00:05:28,108
一张表格放在同一个 chunk 里
A table stays in one chunk.

78
00:05:28,428 --> 00:05:31,828
只有比上限还大的表格才会被切开
Only a table bigger than the cap is split,

79
00:05:31,828 --> 00:05:36,444
按行切，每一块都重复表格的第一行
between rows, with its first row repeated on every piece.

80
00:05:36,764 --> 00:05:40,898
长文本在段落或句子之间切开
Long text is split at paragraph or sentence breaks,

81
00:05:40,898 --> 00:05:45,357
目标大约 1,600 个字符，上限 2,800
aiming for about 1,600 characters, with a cap of 2,800.

82
00:05:45,677 --> 00:05:50,299
少于 200 个字符的碎片会并入相邻的 chunk
Scraps under 200 characters are merged into a neighbour.

83
00:05:50,534 --> 00:05:53,655
20 份文档一共切出 232 个 chunk
On all 20 documents this gives 232 chunks.

84
00:05:53,975 --> 00:05:55,619
最长的两份 PDF
The two longest PDFs,

85
00:05:55,619 --> 00:06:01,257
也就是项目指南和 Medicare 手册，几乎占了一半
the program guide and the Medicare booklet, make up almost half of them.

86
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:04,566
大多数 chunk 远小于目标
Most chunks are far below the target:

87
00:06:04,566 --> 00:06:09,738
中位数大约 850 个字符，因为标题出现得很频繁
the median is about 850 characters, because headings come often.

88
00:06:09,984 --> 00:06:14,524
每个 chunk 存成单独的文件，有自己的 sidecar
Each chunk is stored as its own file, with its own sidecar.

89
00:06:14,844 --> 00:06:18,131
这个 sidecar 必须小于 1 KB
That sidecar must stay under 1 kilobyte:

90
00:06:18,131 --> 00:06:22,898
元数据一旦更大，Bedrock 就会悄悄跳过这个 chunk
Bedrock silently skips any chunk whose metadata is bigger,

91
00:06:22,898 --> 00:06:26,021
却仍然报告任务完成
and still reports the job as complete.

92
00:06:27,067 --> 00:06:31,209
最后一个容器 kb-sync 把每个 chunk 变成一个向量
The last container, kb-sync, turns every chunk into a vector.

93
00:06:31,529 --> 00:06:35,173
一个 embedding 模型，Amazon Titan Text Embeddings v2
An embedding model, Amazon Titan Text Embeddings v2,

94
00:06:35,173 --> 00:06:38,117
读入 chunk，输出 1,024 个数字
reads the chunk and returns 1,024 numbers.

95
00:06:38,437 --> 00:06:42,730
Titan 运行在 Bedrock 上，Bedrock 是亚马逊的一项服务
Titan runs on Bedrock, Amazon's service for using AI models

96
00:06:42,730 --> 00:06:44,914
不用自己部署，就能调用 AI 模型
without running them yourself.

97
00:06:45,150 --> 00:06:49,983
可以把这些数字想成一个有 1,024 个坐标轴的空间里的一个方向
Think of those numbers as a direction in a space with 1,024 axes.

98
00:06:50,303 --> 00:06:54,733
意思相近的 chunk 指向相近的方向
Chunks with similar meaning point in similar directions,

99
00:06:54,733 --> 00:06:59,876
两个方向之间的夹角用余弦相似度（cosine similarity）来衡量
and the angle between two of them, measured by cosine similarity,

100
00:06:59,876 --> 00:07:02,092
检索就靠它来比较
is how search compares them.

101
00:07:02,334 --> 00:07:07,960
这些向量存在一个叫 program-kb 的 S3 Vectors 索引里
The vectors live in an S3 Vectors index, a store built for searching vectors,

102
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:09,627
这是一种专门用来检索向量的存储
called program-kb.

103
00:07:09,947 --> 00:07:12,694
上面是一个 Bedrock Knowledge Base（知识库）
On top sits a Bedrock Knowledge Base

104
00:07:12,694 --> 00:07:15,670
它的数据源就是 chunks 文件夹
whose data source is the chunks folder.

105
00:07:15,990 --> 00:07:18,609
知识库自带的切块功能是关掉的
Its own chunking is switched off,

106
00:07:18,609 --> 00:07:22,896
因为我们自己的 chunk 容器已经做完了这件事
because our chunk container has already done that job.

107
00:07:23,134 --> 00:07:27,779
kb-sync 启动一个导入任务（ingestion job），并等它完成
kb-sync starts an ingestion job and waits for it to finish.

108
00:07:28,099 --> 00:07:32,695
然后它把知识库的 ID 写进 bucket
Then it writes the knowledge base's ID into the bucket,

109
00:07:32,695 --> 00:07:36,456
retrieve 容器就是靠这个找到知识库的
which is how the retrieve container finds it.

110
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,144
为什么选 S3 Vectors？
Why S3 Vectors?

111
00:07:38,194 --> 00:07:46,187
它每月只要几美分，而其他方案每月起步大约 45 或 175 美元
It costs cents a month, while the alternatives start at about 45 or 175 dollars a month.

112
00:07:46,507 --> 00:07:52,911
代价是速度：每次检索大约十分之一到三分之一秒
The price is speed: about a tenth to a third of a second per search,

113
00:07:52,911 --> 00:07:57,715
而在电话里，每十分之一秒都很重要
and on a phone call every tenth of a second counts.

114
00:07:58,750 --> 00:08:01,916
整条 pipeline 贯穿着两个习惯
Two habits run through the whole pipeline.

115
00:08:02,236 --> 00:08:07,914
每个容器只管 bucket 里属于自己的那个文件夹，不碰别人的
Each container owns one folder of the bucket and leaves the others alone.

116
00:08:08,234 --> 00:08:11,922
而且每个容器都会跳过已经做完的工作
And each one skips work that is already done,

117
00:08:11,922 --> 00:08:15,692
所以整个重跑一遍既便宜又安全
so running everything again is cheap and safe.

118
00:08:15,933 --> 00:08:17,430
那么，还有哪些问题没解决？
Now, what is open.

119
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:21,150
做这期视频时，我们发现了三件事
Three things turned up while we made this video.

120
00:08:21,470 --> 00:08:23,948
第一，退伍军人事务部的居家
First, one page, Veterans Affairs'

121
00:08:23,948 --> 00:08:26,965
与社区服务（Home and Community Based Services）页面
Home and Community Based Services,

122
00:08:26,965 --> 00:08:31,409
经过 extract 之后几乎只剩下网站菜单
comes out of extract as little more than the site menu.

123
00:08:31,729 --> 00:08:36,333
它的服务列表放在一个叫 flex-menu 的元素里
Its list of services sits in an element named flex-menu,

124
00:08:36,333 --> 00:08:40,115
而删除菜单的规则把它整个扔掉了
and the rule that strips menus throws it away.

125
00:08:40,350 --> 00:08:42,376
第二，两份来源互相矛盾
Second, two sources disagree.

126
00:08:42,696 --> 00:08:46,912
JACC 网页说服务上限是每月 1,156 美元
The JACC web page caps services at 1,156 dollars a month.

127
00:08:47,232 --> 00:08:49,977
州政府 2026 年的项目对照表
The state's 2026 side-by-side table,

128
00:08:49,977 --> 00:08:53,637
以及团队据此整理的摘要，写的却是 1,090
and the team's summary built from it, say 1,090.

129
00:08:53,957 --> 00:08:58,650
两份都是 2026 年的，所以“优先用最新年份”这条规则也没法裁定
Both are 2026, so "prefer the newest year" cannot settle it.

130
00:08:58,883 --> 00:09:02,450
第三，同一张表格把项目名称藏起来了
Third, that same table hides its program names.

131
00:09:02,770 --> 00:09:06,660
项目名称在 extract 之后还在，就在表格的第二行
They survive extraction, in the table's second row.

132
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:12,490
但 chunk 容器切分大表格时，只重复第一行
But when the chunker splits a big table, it repeats only the first row.

133
00:09:12,810 --> 00:09:17,183
所以装着 1,090 美元的那个 chunk 里，根本没有 JACC 这个词
So the chunk that holds 1,090 dollars never says JACC.

134
00:09:17,417 --> 00:09:23,139
当天晚上的更新：Marco 的分支处理了第 3 个问题
An update from the same evening: Marco's branch works on open item 3.

135
00:09:23,459 --> 00:09:28,134
他的新切块器会重复写着项目名称的那一行，我们验证过
Its new chunker repeats the row with the program names,

136
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:32,978
写着 1,090 美元的那个 chunk 现在包含 JACC
and we checked that the 1,090 dollar chunk now says JACC.

137
00:09:33,298 --> 00:09:37,336
但他新写的表格读取器在真实 PDF 上失败了
But his new table reader fails on the real PDF,

138
00:09:37,336 --> 00:09:41,889
而 retrieve 现在会丢掉这张表里没被验证过的 chunk
and retrieve now drops the table's unverified chunks,

139
00:09:41,889 --> 00:09:46,442
所以目前这张表根本到不了 agent 手里
so for now the table does not reach the agent at all.

140
00:09:46,762 --> 00:09:49,895
第 1、2 个问题在他的分支上没有变化
Open items 1 and 2 are unchanged there.

141
00:09:50,215 --> 00:09:52,458
细节见第 6 集
Episode 6 has the details.

142
00:09:52,700 --> 00:09:57,575
另外还没解决的：目前没有任何机制定期重跑这条 pipeline
Also open: nothing re-runs this pipeline on a schedule yet,

143
00:09:57,575 --> 00:10:01,045
团队的摘要也是手动更新的
and the team's summary is updated by hand.

144
00:10:01,283 --> 00:10:03,923
三个问题，检验一下自己
Three questions to test yourself.

145
00:10:04,243 --> 00:10:09,146
